An infinitely long straight wire carrying current $I$ is bent in a planar shape as shown in the diagram. The radius of the circular part is $r$. The magnetic field at the centre $O$ of the circular loop is:
<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 650 360" width="100%" height="100%">
  <defs>
    <!-- Arrow marker for wire currents and axes -->
    <marker id="arrow" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="6" refY="5" markerWidth="6" markerHeight="6" orient="auto">
      <path d="M 0 1.5 L 9 5 L 0 8.5 Z" fill="#111111"/>
    </marker>
    <!-- Mid-stroke arrow for circular path and straight wire -->
    <marker id="arrow-mid" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="5" refY="5" markerWidth="6" markerHeight="6" orient="auto">
      <path d="M 1 2 L 8 5 L 1 8 Z" fill="#111111"/>
    </marker>
  </defs>

  <style>
    .wire {
      fill: none;
      stroke: #111111;
      stroke-width: 2.2;
      stroke-linecap: round;
      stroke-linejoin: round;
    }
    .axis {
      stroke: #111111;
      stroke-width: 1.8;
      fill: none;
    }
    .radius-line {
      stroke: #111111;
      stroke-width: 1.8;
    }
    .dot {
      fill: #111111;
    }
    .label-math {
      font-family: "Times New Roman", Times, serif;
      font-style: italic;
      font-size: 24px;
      fill: #111111;
      text-anchor: middle;
      dominant-baseline: central;
    }
    .label-text {
      font-family: "Times New Roman", Times, serif;
      font-size: 24px;
      fill: #111111;
      text-anchor: middle;
      dominant-baseline: central;
    }
    .unit-vector {
      font-family: "Times New Roman", Times, serif;
      font-size: 22px;
      fill: #111111;
    }
  </style>

  <!-- Background -->
  <rect width="650" height="360" fill="#ffffff"/>

  <!-- ================= CURRENT LOOP & WIRE ================= -->
  <!-- Straight wire: A -> B -->
  <line x1="50" y1="270" x2="230" y2="270" class="wire" />
  <!-- Arrow on AB -->
  <line x1="120" y1="270" x2="135" y2="270" class="wire" marker-end="url(#arrow)" />

  <!-- Straight wire: D -> E -->
  <line x1="270" y1="270" x2="450" y2="270" class="wire" />
  <!-- Arrow on DE -->
  <line x1="340" y1="270" x2="355" y2="270" class="wire" marker-end="url(#arrow)" />

  <!-- Circular loop: starts near B (230,270), loops around center (250, 170) with radius R = 100 -->
  <!-- Gap at bottom between ~101.5 deg and ~78.5 deg (relative to standard circle coords where 90 is bottom) -->
  <path d="M 230 270 
           A 100 100 0 1 1 270 270" 
        class="wire" />

  <!-- Arrow at the top of the loop (Point C) pointing clockwise (right) -->
  <line x1="245" y1="70" x2="256" y2="70" class="wire" marker-end="url(#arrow)" />

  <!-- Center Point O -->
  <circle cx="250" cy="170" r="4.5" class="dot" />

  <!-- Radius line from center O to upper-right arc -->
  <line x1="250" y1="170" x2="321" y2="99" class="radius-line" />

  <!-- ================= LABELS (LOOP & WIRE) ================= -->
  <!-- Wire vertices -->
  <text x="50" y="300" class="label-math">A</text>
  <text x="225" y="300" class="label-math">B</text>
  <text x="275" y="300" class="label-math">D</text>
  <text x="445" y="300" class="label-math">E</text>
  <text x="235" y="180" class="label-math">O</text>
  <text x="250" y="50" class="label-math">C</text>

  <!-- Current labels -->
  <text x="127" y="300" class="label-math">I</text>
  <text x="250" y="95" class="label-math">I</text>
  <text x="347" y="300" class="label-math">I</text>

  <!-- Radius label -->
  <text x="270" y="125" class="label-math">r</text>

  <!-- ================= 3D COORDINATE SYSTEM ================= -->
  <!-- Origin at (430, 125) -->
  <!-- Z-axis (upward) -->
  <line x1="430" y1="125" x2="430" y2="45" class="axis" marker-end="url(#arrow)" />

  <!-- Y-axis (rightward) -->
  <line x1="430" y1="125" x2="510" y2="125" class="axis" marker-end="url(#arrow)" />

  <!-- X-axis (down-left) -->
  <line x1="430" y1="125" x2="375" y2="180" class="axis" marker-end="url(#arrow)" />

  <!-- Coordinate Labels -->
  <!-- z (k_hat) -->
  <text x="448" y="45" class="label-math">z</text>
  <text x="462" y="45" class="unit-vector">(k&#770;)</text>

  <!-- y (j_hat) -->
  <text x="530" y="127" class="label-math">y</text>
  <text x="544" y="127" class="unit-vector">(j&#770;)</text>

  <!-- x (i_hat) -->
  <text x="375" y="202" class="label-math">x</text>
  <text x="389" y="202" class="unit-vector">(i&#770;)</text>
</svg>

As shown in the diagram, when the incident ray is parallel to base of the prism, the emergent ray grazes along the second surface. If refractive index of the material of prism is $\sqrt{2}$, the angle $\theta$ of prism is.
<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 550 300" width="100%" height="100%">
  <defs>
    <!-- Arrowhead marker -->
    <marker id="arrow" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="6" refY="5" markerWidth="7" markerHeight="7" orient="auto-start-reverse">
      <path d="M 1 1.5 L 8 5 L 1 8.5" fill="none" stroke="#000" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/>
    </marker>
  </defs>

  <style>
    .label {
      font-family: "Times New Roman", Times, Georgia, serif;
      font-size: 24px;
      fill: #000;
    }
    .line {
      stroke: #000;
      stroke-width: 2.2;
      stroke-linecap: round;
      stroke-linejoin: round;
    }
    .ray {
      stroke: #000;
      stroke-width: 2;
      fill: none;
    }
    .arc {
      fill: none;
      stroke: #000;
      stroke-width: 1.8;
    }
  </style>

  <!-- Prism outline -->
  <polygon points="170,240 360,30 475,240" fill="none" class="line" />

  <!-- Angle arcs -->
  <!-- 45 degree arc at left vertex (170, 240) -->
  <path d="M 210,240 A 40 40 0 0 0 197,210" class="arc" />

  <!-- theta arc at right vertex (475, 240) -->
  <path d="M 440,240 A 35 35 0 0 1 458,208" class="arc" />

  <!-- Light Ray segments -->
  <!-- 1. Incident ray before prism -->
  <line x1="50" y1="105" x2="135" y2="105" class="ray" marker-end="url(#arrow)" />
  <line x1="130" y1="105" x2="295" y2="105" class="ray" />

  <!-- 2. Refracted ray inside prism -->
  <line x1="295" y1="105" x2="350" y2="110" class="ray" marker-end="url(#arrow)" />
  <line x1="345" y1="109.5" x2="405" y2="115" class="ray" />

  <!-- 3. Ray traveling along right surface -->
  <line x1="405" y1="115" x2="445" y2="186" class="ray" marker-end="url(#arrow)" />
  <line x1="440" y1="177" x2="475" y2="240" class="ray" />

  <!-- Labels -->
  <text x="115" y="75" text-anchor="middle" class="label">Incident ray</text>
  <text x="235" y="215" text-anchor="middle" class="label">45°</text>
  <text x="430" y="222" text-anchor="middle" class="label" font-style="italic">θ</text>
  <text x="322" y="275" text-anchor="middle" class="label">Base</text>
</svg>

A biconvex lens is formed by using two thin planoconvex lenses, as shown in the figure. The refractive index and radius of curved surfaces are also mentioned in figure. When an object is placed on the left side of lens at a distance of $30\text{ cm}$ from the biconvex lens, the magnification of the image will be:
<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 450 360" width="100%" height="100%">
  <defs>
    <!-- Arrowhead marker -->
    <marker id="arrow" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="7" refY="5" markerWidth="6" markerHeight="6" orient="auto-start-reverse">
      <path d="M 0 1.5 L 8 5 L 0 8.5 z" fill="#000" />
    </marker>
  </defs>

  <style>
    .label {
      font-family: "Times New Roman", Times, Georgia, serif;
      font-size: 28px;
      fill: #000;
      text-anchor: middle;
      dominant-baseline: middle;
    }
    .lens-outline {
      stroke: #000;
      stroke-width: 2.5;
      fill: none;
    }
    .divider {
      stroke: #000;
      stroke-width: 2;
      stroke-dasharray: 6 5;
    }
    .pointer {
      stroke: #000;
      stroke-width: 2;
      fill: none;
      marker-end: url(#arrow);
    }
  </style>

  <!-- Lens Outline -->
  <!-- Left curved boundary -->
  <path d="M 225,50 A 35 125 0 0 0 225,300" class="lens-outline" />

  <!-- Right curved boundary -->
  <path d="M 225,50 A 35 125 0 0 1 225,300" class="lens-outline" />

  <!-- Center dashed line divider -->
  <line x1="225" y1="50" x2="225" y2="300" class="divider" />

  <!-- Top-Left: μ = 1.5 -->
  <text x="110" y="40" class="label">μ = 1.5</text>
  <line x1="150" y1="55" x2="210" y2="115" class="pointer" />

  <!-- Top-Right: μ = 1.2 -->
  <text x="340" y="40" class="label">μ = 1.2</text>
  <line x1="300" y1="55" x2="240" y2="115" class="pointer" />

  <!-- Bottom-Left: 15 cm -->
  <text x="110" y="325" class="label">15 cm</text>
  <line x1="145" y1="300" x2="200" y2="245" class="pointer" />

  <!-- Bottom-Right: 12 cm -->
  <text x="340" y="325" class="label">12 cm</text>
  <line x1="305" y1="300" x2="250" y2="245" class="pointer" />
</svg>
